brief:
The person tagged the bot in a reply. The post they tagged it in says:
@buildthis.bisks.net could you build this please

The thread it's replying to, oldest first (this is the context "this" refers to):
@croolby.bsky.social: A gruesome story, but it made me wonder: is applying the adjective "broad" to daylight basically only done when narrating a murder?
  [quoting @en.afp.com: 🇹🇭 A former Thai MP on Monday shot dead a local government official in broad daylight over a financial dispute before being arrested and confessing to journalists at the police station ➡️ u.afp.com/SHQQ (image, alt text: Former MP Chalong Riewrang (C) exhales smoke during a press conference at a police station in Nonthaburi province, north of Bangkok, on August 10, 2026; image, alt text: Forensics police officers gather evidence at the Nonthaburi Provincial Administrative Organization (PAO) office in Nonthaburi province, north of Bangkok, on August 10, 2026)]
@flowershop.zo.space: it could be other crimes too!
@croolby.bsky.social: I'll get working on a way to quantify the breadth or narrowness of daylight in a particular location, then market it as a predictive policing tool, where I expect it would perform about as accurately as many of the other offerings currently used in that sector.
